🏠 Housing Price Prediction

📌 Project Overview

This project predicts the price of a house based on different features such as area, number of bedrooms, bathrooms, house age, parking spaces, floor, distance from the city, and location score.

🎯 Objective

The main objective is to build a Machine Learning model that can predict house prices accurately using historical housing data.

📊 Dataset

The dataset contains 3,000 records and 9 columns.

Features:

- "Area_sqft" – Area of the house in square feet
- "Bedrooms" – Number of bedrooms
- "Bathrooms" – Number of bathrooms
- "House_Age_years" – Age of the house
- "Parking_Spaces" – Number of parking spaces
- "Floor" – Floor number
- "Distance_from_City_km" – Distance from city center
- "Location_Score" – Location quality score

Target:

- "Price" – Predicted house price

🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn
- Google Colab

🤖 Machine Learning Models

1. Linear Regression
2. Random Forest Regression

🔄 Project Workflow

Dataset → Data Cleaning → Data Analysis → Feature Selection → Train/Test Split → Model Training → Prediction → Model Evaluation

📈 Evaluation Metrics

The models are evaluated using:

- MAE (Mean Absolute Error)
- MSE (Mean Squared Error)
- RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)
- R² Score

🚀 Future Improvements

- Use a larger real-world housing dataset
- Apply advanced regression algorithms
- Perform hyperparameter tuning
- Build a web application for real-time house price prediction

